  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solar Soaker</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Solar Soaker is a laundry tool that uses the heat of the sun to remove stains and dirt without a need for hand washing.The objective of this DGGF-TA supported project is to (1) investigate the viability of a launderette business model in Uganda, and (2) investigating the viability of healthy entrepreneurs as local distribution and marketing partner, and investigate if local manufacturing partners can produce the solar soaker tool. The local sub-contracted partner is research &amp; ideation agency Dr. Monk, who contributes skills such as end-user research to generate deep insights including cultural fit, as well as doing ideation/co-creation sessions.The project created 3 pilot locations with launderette and laundromats, and has improved the quality of work for informal laundry workers that were involved in the project. Partner organization Healthy Entrepreneurs takes care of the distribution of the detergent which is needed for the Solar Soaker. During this pilot, the dobbies, the people who do laundry for a living, make use of the Solar Soaker, which increases their work capacity and creates better paid jobs for the dobbies. During this pilot, a little over 19 indirect FTE were supported and 18 people were trained in the use of the system.</narrative>
  </description>
